From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op pane text wrap: the texts the game sets in its text
 panes, to the module

One more wrapped game function in patch 0005's table
(nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; its id in host/hos_coop_pane_text.h), for
the module's play-test bridge (oot-remake-multiplayer's docs/playtest.md
"Text boxes"):
- 25: main+0x439520, a text pane's set-message call (pane, &{text, length}).
The text box keeps the pointer, not a copy, so the module copies the text
at the call. Phase 0 only reads. Nothing else changes: the wrap machinery,
the checks (build id, first words) and the hello's bits are 0005's.
---
 host/hos_coop_pane_text.h | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 nx2/coop_world_wraps.py   |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 host/hos_coop_pane_text.h

diff --git a/host/hos_coop_pane_text.h b/host/hos_coop_pane_text.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..63d6e30
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/hos_coop_pane_text.h
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+   The texts the game puts in its text panes, for the play-test bridge (oot-remake-multiplayer, docs/playtest.md "Text
+   boxes").
+
+   One wrapped game function more in the one wrap table (patch 0005's nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; the ids are in
+   the one wrap space of hos_coop_world.h). Patch 0037 adds its row and this file (Hookshot's host/hos_coop_pane_text.h
+   is the same file). The module's hos_coop_wrap gets it; Hookshot announces it in HOS_COOP_WORLD_HELLO's bits. The row:
+     (25, 0x439520, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bd7bfd, 0xf9000bf5, 0xa9024ff4)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; str x21; stp x20, x19
+   Phase 0 only reads (never skips): x0 the pane (0xb0 bytes in its layout's array), x1 a reference {+0 the text,
+   +8 its length in bytes, +0x10 the attributes}; the text box keeps the pointer, not a copy. Plain C. */
+#ifndef HOS_COOP_PANE_TEXT_H
+#define HOS_COOP_PANE_TEXT_H
+
+/* main+0x439520, a text pane's set-message call: every text the game shows in a layout's text pane (the message
+   window's line and speaker, menus, the HUD) goes through it. */
+#define HOS_COOP_WRAP_PANE_TEXT 25u
+
+#endif
diff --git a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
index 20aca8a..8cea7e3 100644
--- a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
+++ b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
@@ -52,6 +52,11 @@ WRAPS = (
     # main+0x4ba4a28 slot 29, only called through it), which only Game Over's graphs run (Retry: Try Again,
     # EventToTitle: Quit Game). A save load after it with no title menu between is Try Again. Phase 0 reads only
     (9, 0x32bbce0, (0xd503237f, 0xa9be7bfd, 0xf9000bf3, 0x910003fd)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; str x19; mov x29, sp
+    # HOS_COOP_WRAP_PANE_TEXT (patch 0037): a text pane's set-message call (x0 the pane, x1 a reference {+0 the text,
+    # +8 its length in bytes}): every text the game shows in a layout's text pane, the message window's too. The text
+    # box keeps the pointer, so the module copies the text at the call, for the play-test bridge only
+    # (oot-remake-multiplayer's docs/playtest.md "Text boxes"). Phase 0 reads only, never skips
+    (25, 0x439520, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bd7bfd, 0xf9000bf5, 0xa9024ff4)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; str x21; stp x20, x19
 )
 
 
